# gmsh third-party manifest (M287-A spike governance)

name: gmsh
version: 4.15.2
distribution: PyPI wheel "gmsh" (bundled gmsh SDK shared library + Python API)
license: GPL-2.0-or-later (see third_party/licenses/gmsh-LICENSE-NOTE.md)
upstream: https://gmsh.info

status: production python preprocessing (python/scau_preproc/meshgen.py, M287-B)
  under the same subprocess isolation as the spike. NOT part of the main CMake
  graph, NOT linked by any production target, NOT vendored into extern/.
  Pinned with numpy/netCDF4/pyproj in third_party/manifest/preproc-python.lock.

isolation policy:
  - gmsh is imported only inside the mesh-generation subprocess
    (python/scau_preproc/meshgen.py; spike precedent spikes/gmsh_meshgen). The subprocess boundary is both
    the fault-isolation boundary (timeout kill, no partial output) and the
    GPL license boundary; the C++ core and any future orchestration layer
    communicate with it exclusively through files (JSON config in,
    .stcf.nc + reports out).
  - production adoption (M287-B) must keep the same subprocess isolation or
    complete a license review before any in-process linking.

determinism policy:
  - pinned options: Mesh.Algorithm=6, Mesh.RandomSeed=1,
    General.NumThreads=1, Blossom recombination;
  - same-platform rerun bitwise output equality is required evidence for
    every version bump of this manifest.
  - cross-platform (B7): every GoldenSuite preproc fixture (G30/G32/G36/G37/G38)
    is SAME-PLATFORM evidence (Windows x86_64, this manifest). The CI lane
    `preproc-cross-platform` (ubuntu, preproc-python.lock) regenerates G30 with
    tools/preproc/cross_platform_hash.py and uploads a verdict row to
    third_party/compatibility/b7_evidence/ via artifact; the lane is
    evidence-collecting (non-blocking) until the B7 decision fixes the gate
    wording ("bitwise" vs "recorded 1e-12 tolerance").
